==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|jār|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*jērą}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*yōr-}} < {{m|ine-pro|*yeh₁r-}}. Compare Dutch {{term|jaar|lang=nl}}, English {{term|year|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|år|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/jaːɐ̯/|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|/jaː/|lang=de}} {{a|common}}
* {{audio|De-Jahr.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aːɐ̯|lang=de}}
* {{homophones|ja|lang=de}} {{qualifier|nonstandard}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Jahres|gen2=Jahrs|Jahre|pl2=Jahr|Jährchen}}

# [[year]]

====Usage notes====
* The normal plural is '''Jahre'''.
* The unchanged plural ''Jahr'' is rare in formal prose, but may be seen in colloquial or poetic language. It is used chiefly after numerals, most often in adverbial constructions such as ''zwei Jahr später'' (“two years later”).

